Project Mu: harden privacy defaults

Default-value changes only; every setting stays user-adjustable in Settings:

  * profile.cookie_controls_mode -> kBlockThirdParty
    (third-party cookies blocked in normal windows, not only Incognito)
  * enable_do_not_track -> true (send the DNT header)
  * webrtc.ip_handling_policy -> default_public_interface_only
    (WebRTC keeps working, but pages cannot read local LAN IP addresses)
  * https_only_mode_enabled -> true ("Always use secure connections")
  * enable_a_ping -> false (no <a ping> hyperlink-auditing beacons)
  * search.suggest_enabled -> false (keystrokes in the address bar are not
    sent to the search engine)
  * background_mode.enabled -> false (Windows/Linux: the browser exits when
    the last window closes, so 0004's clear-on-exit actually runs)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/background/extensions/background_mode_manager.cc b/chrome/browser/background/extensions/background_mode_manager.cc
index 16e28b4..819e4b6 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/background/extensions/background_mode_manager.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/background/extensions/background_mode_manager.cc
@@ -351,7 +351,9 @@ BackgroundModeManager::~BackgroundModeManager() {
 
 // static
 void BackgroundModeManager::RegisterPrefs(PrefRegistrySimple* registry) {
-  registry->RegisterBooleanPref(prefs::kBackgroundModeEnabled, true);
+  // Project Mu: do not keep running in the background after the last window
+  // closes, so the session really ends (and clear-on-exit runs) on close.
+  registry->RegisterBooleanPref(prefs::kBackgroundModeEnabled, false);
 }
 
 void BackgroundModeManager::RegisterProfile(Profile* profile) {
